     3,
     "<br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">Terrence Jorgensen schrieb am Donnerstag, 24. September 2020 um 12:37:39 UTC+2:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div>errors like this one:</div><div><br></div><div><font color=\"#ff0000\">Error in .local(object, ...) : unused argument (standardized = FALSE)</font></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>&quot;like this&quot; is pretty vague.  Any other clues?  This error makes it look like your R is not finding the correct<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> summary() </font>method for lavaan.mi objects, which does have a<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> standardized= </font>argument.  Does it recognize &quot;test&quot; as lavaan.mi?</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#008\">class</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">test</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div></div><div><br></div><div>Also run<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> sessionInfo() </font>to show us what versions of the software you are using.  My output shows:</div><div><br></div><div style=\"border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">R version </span><span style=\"color:#066\">4.0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">...</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>other attached packages</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mice_3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">11.0</span><span style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><span style=\"color:#000\">        </span></span><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,0)\"><span style=\"color:#000\">semTools_0</span></span><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,0)\"><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3.910</span></span><span style=\"color:#000\"> tables_0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">9.6</span><span style=\"color:#000\">       </span><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,0)\"><span style=\"color:#000\">lavaan_0</span></span><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,0)\"><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">7</span></span><span style=\"color:#000\">      <br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ggplot2_3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3.2</span><span style=\"color:#000\">      foreign_0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">8</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">80</span><span style=\"color:#000\">     openxlsx_4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.5</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    <br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">...</span></div></code></div><div><br>If you have older versions, make sure the errors still occur after installing the latest development version of semTools in a fresh version of R, using the devtools package:</div><div><br></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">devtools</span><span style=\"color:#660\">::</span><span style=\"color:#000\">install_github</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;simsem/semTools/semTools&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><div><br>Then restart R before loading (only) semTools and mice to run your script.</div><div><br></div><div>Without supplying data with your syntax, it is not a reproducible example.  Can you run the<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> ?runMI </font>help-page examples?  Granted, those are all single-level models, but here is a two-level model (with level-2 predictors, like you have) example that I can run fine:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">dat2 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> lapply</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">m</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    dat </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> lavaan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">::</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Demo</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">twolevel<br>    dat$y1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> runif</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># so there is some between-imputation variance</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    dat<br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">})</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># 3 &quot;imputed&quot; data sets</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>model </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;<br>    level: 1<br>        fw =~ y1 + y2 + y3<br>        fw ~ x1 + x2 + x3<br>    level: 2<br>        fb =~ y1 + y2 + y3<br>        fb ~ w1 + w2<br>&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>fit </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sem</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mi</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> dat2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> cluster </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;cluster&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>summary</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><div><br></div></div><div>If you can&#39;t run that, then please provide additional syntax and any errors you see.</div><div><br></div><div><div><div>Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div>Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics</div><div>Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div><a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"ht